+
+**What an attempt is told.** The deployment publishes one read-only
+`handoff.json` beside `task.json` (`baton.native-handoff-context/1`) whenever
+the Job's template has a handoff branch: a fresh implementer learns the
+configured recipient; a reviewer over a yielded checkpoint learns the pending
+request and the checkpoint it is about; a resumed implementer learns the exact
+question it stopped at and the exact reply, read back from the Authority by the
+identities the committed continuation names. Workers never see a host store.
+
+**What a reply earns.** The reviewer's `response` is a clarification or
+discovery interpretation and never an accepted technical review: it mints no
+verification, review, approval or integration receipt, and the review stage
+projects `answered` rather than `completed`, so the integration's gate stays
+shut. An `answer` is committed as the one reply to the exact pending request
+(by identity and by digest), earns a recorded `continuation` effect, holds the
+line for one continuation writer, and `advance_continuation` opens fresh
+episodes for both stages under the Job's own continuation allowance — spending
+no correction round and moving no deadline. An `escalate` earns a recorded
+`held` effect addressed to the configured decision recipient (never the same
+reviewer), is journalled once per yielding episode (`native.hold`) and reread
+on every later tick rather than raised again, and leaves the execution held.
+
+**Configuration.** The Authority policy `native_handoff_routing`
+(`baton.native-handoff-routing/1`: `reviewer`, `decision_recipient`, which may
+not be one address) and the `answer-handoff` capability granted to the
+reviewer in the Work's effective scope; the control profile `native-handoff/1`
+(every ceiling of `documentation/1`, zero correction rounds, ONE resolved
+continuation). A handoff-capable Job in a deployment with no routing is refused
+at preparation, before a provider turn is spent. The worker image must carry
+this revision's adapter; an older image refuses a declared `handoff` output
+by name. Authority schema version 7 adds `work_message` and
+`work_message_transition`; a retained store at 6 is refused, not migrated.
